Hi Mike,

Hope everything goes well!

I have several questions about the very
cool micro_era5 function.

I notice that the micro_era5
function contains two parameters that allow uniformly adjusting hourly
temperatures ('warm') and daily precipitation. Can I use them to simulate
climate change? Say, for each site, I calculate the predicted changes of
temperature and precipitation from WorldClim, and use them for the two
parameters in micro_era5?

What I found hard to understand was
that the "rainoff" reduced daily rainfall to a negative value if the
'rainoff' was less than zero, and the magnitude of ‘rainoff’ was larger than
current rainfall. I also found that the 'rainoff' not only affected rainfall
but also temperatures. Even when the daily rainfall was reduced from 0 to a
negative value, it would affect temperatures. Given these, does the ‘rainoff’ still
produce meaningful simulation of changes in precipitation (and corresponding effects
on temperatures)?

Your answer will be most
appreciated!

All the best,

Liang

